    \"HTML\",
    \"CSS\",
    \"JavaScript\",
    \"Bootstrap\",
    \"PDF\"
  ],
  \"grading_criteria\": [
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Testing Scope\",
      \"feedback\": \"The learner has clearly defined the testing scope in the report, including all required website areas such as the Homepage, Destinations page, Tour Packages page, Navigation bar, Cross-page links, Destination cards, Package cards, Booking inquiry form, Responsive layout testing, Browser compatibility testing, and Lighthouse testing. The explanation of why testing is important before deployment is also well-articulated.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The testing scope is comprehensive and meets all requirements.\",
      \"score\": \"10 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Test Plan Preparation\",
      \"feedback\": \"The test plan is well-prepared and presented in a clear table format, as required. It effectively outlines the features to be tested, the testing types (functional, validation, browser, responsive, Lighthouse), and the expected results for each. This demonstrates a solid understanding of test planning principles.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The test plan preparation is excellent.\",
      \"score\": \"10 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Functional Testing Results\",
      \"feedback\": \"The learner has thoroughly tested and documented the functional aspects of the website, including the Homepage, Destinations page, Tour Packages page, Navigation links, Navigation consistency, Destination cards, Package cards, Buttons, and Links. Each test includes the expected result, actual result, and a PASS/FAIL status. The provided screenshots in the report (pages 7-8) visually confirm the correct loading and display of these elements. The underlying HTML structure in `index.html`, `destinations.html`, and `packages.html` supports the claimed functionality, with correct navigation links and card structures.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The functional testing results are comprehensive and well-supported.\",
      \"score\": \"20 / 20\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Booking Inquiry Form Validation Testing\",
      \"feedback\": \"The report details comprehensive testing for the booking inquiry form's validation rules, covering blank fields, email format, password matching, contact number format, booking reference ID, and successful submission. The table clearly lists expected results, actual results, and PASS/FAIL statuses. The attached screenshots (pages 10-11) effectively demonstrate both failed validation messages and a successful submission alert. The `script.js` file contains robust JavaScript logic for `validateRequired`, email validation (`!email.includes(\\\"@\\\")`), password matching (`password !== confirmPassword`), contact number validation (`isNaN(contact)`), and booking reference ID validation (`!bookingRef.startsWith(\\\"TV-\\\")`), along with form reset on success, all of which align perfectly with the assignment requirements.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The form validation testing is excellent and fully implemented.\",
      \"score\": \"15 / 15\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Cross-Browser Compatibility Testing\",
      \"feedback\": \"The learner has documented cross-browser compatibility testing for Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Mozilla Firefox, indicating 'PASS' for all. However, the submission lacks specific visual evidence, such as distinct screenshots for each browser, to support these claims. While the report states the website functions correctly across browsers, concrete visual proof for each browser is a mandatory requirement for full marks.\",
      \"fixing\": \"To improve, include separate screenshots for each required browser (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Mozilla Firefox) demonstrating that pages load correctly, navigation works, and the layout displays as expected in each specific browser environment. This visual evidence is crucial to fully meet the assignment's requirements.\",
      \"score\": \"5 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Responsive Layout Testing\",
      \"feedback\": \"The responsive layout testing is well-documented, covering mobile, tablet, and desktop views. The report includes a table summarizing the results and provides clear screenshots for each required view (Mobile View on page 13, Ipad View on page 14, Laptop View on page 15). These visuals confirm that the navbar behavior, text readability, image responsiveness, and card alignment adapt correctly across different screen sizes, demonstrating a functional responsive design.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The responsive layout testing is thorough and well-evidenced.\",
      \"score\": \"10 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Lighthouse Testing\",
      \"feedback\": \"The learner has successfully performed Lighthouse testing, providing the required Performance (81/100), Accessibility (91/100), Best Practices (95/100), and SEO (100/100) scores. A clear Lighthouse screenshot is included in the report (page 16). The 'Final Testing Summary' section (page 17) provides a concise analysis of these scores and includes a recommendation for optimizing image assets to improve performance, fulfilling all requirements for this task.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The Lighthouse testing is complete and well-documented.\",
      \"score\": \"10 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Testing Evidence & Screenshots\",
      \"feedback\": \"The submission includes a good range of relevant screenshots supporting the functional, validation, responsive, and Lighthouse testing results. The quality of the screenshots is generally high, and they effectively demonstrate the tested functionalities. However, the absence of specific screenshots for each browser during the cross-browser compatibility testing (as noted in the 'Cross-Browser Compatibility Testing' section) leads to a minor deduction, as comprehensive visual evidence for all testing types was expected.\",
      \"fixing\": \"Ensure that all required testing types, especially cross-browser compatibility, are supported by distinct visual evidence. For instance, include a separate screenshot for each browser tested to visually confirm the website's consistent appearance and functionality.\",
      \"score\": \"8 / 10\"
    },
    {
      \"criteria\": \"Final Testing Documentation Report\",
      \"feedback\": \"The final testing documentation report is well-structured and organized. It includes all required sections such as a cover title, testing scope, test plan, detailed results for functional, form validation, cross-browser, responsive, and Lighthouse testing, and a comprehensive final summary. The report uses clear headings, tables where appropriate, and consistent PASS/FAIL statuses, making it easy to read and understand. The explanations are beginner-friendly, meeting all specified report requirements.\",
      \"fixing\": \"No fixing required. The final testing documentation report is well-prepared and meets all organizational and formatting requirements.\",
      \"score\": \"5 / 5\"
    }
  ],
  \"detected_files\": [
